   384	errors, both conceded.
   385	(a) *Arithmetic (O3).* Apers–Gribling–Sen–Szabó, *Quantum* 7, 1202 (2023),
   386	DOI 10.22331/q-2023-12-06-1202, arXiv:2211.09618, estimate the `k`-th normalised Betti number
   387	of a simplicial complex to additive `eps` in `n^{O(gamma^{-1/2} log(1/eps))}`, `gamma` the
   388	combinatorial-Laplacian gap. At `gamma = Omega(1)` **and constant `eps`** this is polynomial.
   389	At `gamma = Omega(1)` and `eps = 1/poly(n)` it is `n^{O(log n)}` — quasi-polynomial, which
   390	**still permits a super-polynomial separation** from a polynomial quantum algorithm. The r0
   391	sentences "no super-polynomial quantum advantage exists at `gamma = Omega(1)`" and "the only
   392	surviving window is `gamma = 1/poly(n)`" are **withdrawn**.
   393	(b) *Access model (O4).* The theorem is proved for combinatorial Laplacians of simplicial
   394	complexes, using their row structure and bounded path-integral weights. A generic `L_W`
   395	contains the generally dense `P_0`; a QSVT block encoding is not a classical sparse-row oracle;
