   431	**5. Heuristic attack — FAILS: at most a small monomial demonstration.** The full Koszul
   432	Laplacian is the *free* Hamiltonian `N̂ + F̂` (Step 4.1); all content sits in `P_0`, which is
   433	not an interaction, so the generic problem still needs a nonphysical projector. *Survives*, and
   434	with a wording correction (O14): for a **monomial** ideal `H_N` is diagonal (C-111), `P_0` is a
   435	computational-basis projector, and `L_W` is a sparse number-conserving hopping Hamiltonian on
   436	the standard monomials tensored with a Jordan–Wigner fermion register on `n+1` sites. The
   437	smallest demonstration is the Stanley–Reisner ideal of the 4-cycle, `I = (z_0z_2, z_1z_3)`,
   438	block `(i=1,N=1)`: one boson in four modes — a **four-mode path (ququart) encoding, not a
   439	dual-rail encoding** — plus one fermion in four modes, a 16-level two-particle problem with
   440	zero-energy degeneracy `beta_{1,2} = 2`. The 7-cycle at `(i=3,N=1)` is 245-dimensional with
   441	degeneracy 35 and normalised gap 0.146. Second survivor: the generator-Koszul supercharge of
   442	Step 8, a genuine `max_j m_j`-body boson–fermion interaction with no projector whose `i=0`
   443	block is exactly `H_N` (part f) — the only natively physical object this lane found, and it
   444	computes Koszul homology of the sequence, not the Betti table.
