   448	## 4. Killers
   449	
   450	**K-KB1 (support collapse; F3).** `beta_{i,j} = 0` for `j-i > reg(R/I)` (Step 6, part a), so
   451	the useful block label satisfies `N <= reg(R/I)`; the twisted cubic, the rational normal curves
   452	and every determinantal example in the seed's survey have `reg(R/I) <= 2`. It does **not**
   453	preclude large `N` when regularity grows: D-boolean-ideal / D-clause-ideal have
   454	`reg(R/I) = Theta(n)` — and are exactly the #P-hard families. Severity high.
   455	
   456	**K-KB2 (the naive compression is information-free).** `P̂ L P̂ = (N+i) P̂` exactly (Step 4.3,
   457	part b): "block-encode the projected Koszul Laplacian" returns a scalar. `L_W` must be built
   458	from `q^† = sum_k Z_k ⊗ c_k`. Severity decisive for how the operator is presented; see K-KB9
   459	for what it costs, which is **not** unconditionally a QSVT per call (O11).
   460	
   461	**K-KB3 (the squarefree part is quantum TDA; the rest is not).** Hochster plus part d: the
   462	**squarefree multidegree summands** of `L_W` for a Stanley–Reisner ideal are simplicial
   463	Laplacians of induced subcomplexes, so #P-hardness of exact evaluation and NP-hardness of
   464	multiplicative approximation transfer unconditionally (arXiv:2209.14286), and the
   465	Apers et al. estimator applies there. The **non-squarefree** part of the total block is covered
   466	by no cited theorem (part d: 42 of 49, 105 of 147, 7 of 294 dimensions squarefree). Severity
   467	decisive for the speedup, and the source of the HOLD on C-NEW-KB-QMA1.
   468	
   469	**K-KB4 (novelty of the mechanism).** Cade–Crichigno arXiv:2107.00011 own the SUSY/cohomology
   470	Hamiltonian framework *and* DQC1-hardness of normalised Betti estimation on general cochain
   471	complexes; only the algebro-geometric instance is new here. Action: a C-110-style scout on
   472	whether "graded Betti numbers = nullity of a Laplacian built from compressed multiplications on
   473	the Macaulay inverse system" already exists (operator theory, C-015/C-017, or physics).
   474	Severity medium.
   475	
   476	**K-KB5 (the cheap blocks are input data).** `beta_{1,j}` counts minimal generators and
   477	`beta_{1,2} = dim I_2` is a rank (Step 7.3, every family). The first genuinely non-input block
   478	is `i = 2`, where the fraction is `~ n^{-4}` at fixed `c` (part g). Severity medium.
   479	
   480	**K-KB6 (the Betti gap can close while the Macaulay gap does not).** Now with a **proved
   481	infinite counterfamily** (Step 5.6, part e): for the `m`-cycle Stanley–Reisner ideal
   482	`Delta_2 = 1` for every `m` while the squarefree Betti gap is exactly `2-2cos(2 pi/m)`, so no
   483	bound `g >= phi(Delta_N)` exists. `g_{i,N}` is an invariant of the ideal and the metric, **not**
   484	presentation-dependent (O7); its *realisation cost* through `H_N` is what depends on the tuple.
   485	No lower bound on `g` is known for any interesting class. Severity high: the runtime carries
   486	`j/g`.
   487	
   488	**K-KB7 (no hardware hook for `L_W`).** The full Koszul Laplacian is the *free* Hamiltonian
   489	(Step 4.1). Survivors: the monomial-ideal ququart demonstration of §3.5 and the generator-Koszul
   490	Hamiltonian of Step 8, now verified to have the seed `H_N` as its `i=0` block. Severity high
   491	against PRD criterion 5.
   492	
   493	**K-KB8 (output).** Only a normalised fraction is estimable; recovering `beta` needs
   494	`eps < 1/(2 dim)`, which #P-hardness forbids anyway. Severity medium; same kind as C-091/C-093.
   495	
   496	**K-KB9 (access model decides the cost, and preconditioning is symmetric).** Under
   497	generator-only access via `H_N` each `L_W` call inherits `alpha_BE/Delta_N`; under
   498	standard-monomial access (monomial ideals) or a supplied quotient-multiplication oracle it does
   499	not (O11). Whichever access is granted must be granted to the classical baseline too, and the
   500	residual `n log N` qubits versus `M_N` words is refused as a space separation by PRD D15 /
   501	SP-0 (C-264). The arm should make no space claim. Severity high.
   502	
   503	**K-KB10 (regularity, downgraded).** `reg(I)` is worst-case doubly exponential (Mayr–Meyer;
   504	Bayer–Mumford), but it is needed only to **enumerate** the Betti table, not to answer one
   505	requested `(i,j)`; and `reg(R/I) = reg(I) - 1`. Severity downgraded from medium to minor (O1).
   506	
   507	**K-KB11 (NEW at r1: the conditional normalisation is the real overlap wall).** The
   508	`W_N`-conditional fraction costs `M_N/h_N` samples or `sqrt(M_N/h_N)` coherent projections
   509	(Step 9.2, C-096), and `h_N/M_N ≈ rho^{codim}` is exponentially small for every square system
   510	(applications memo caution 1). This is the FATAL objection O2 turned into a killer, and it
   511	supersedes the r0 claim that arm B escaped the overlap trap. Severity decisive.
   512	
   513	**K-KB12 (NEW at r1: the total-block gap is not a clique-complex gap).** `g_{i,N}` is a minimum
   514	over every multidegree in the block, while every cited gapped-clique-homology theorem controls
   515	one simplicial Laplacian (O5). Until the non-squarefree summands are bounded below, neither the
   516	hardness transfer nor the dequantization transfer is licensed at the total-block level.
   517	Severity decisive for C-NEW-KB-QMA1 and C-NEW-KB-DEQUANT.
   518	
