   529	
   530	- **D-fermionic-modes** (ACCEPTED unchanged). `c_k, c_k^†` (`k = 0..n`) on `Lambda(C^{n+1})`
   531	  with `{c_k, c_l^†} = delta_{kl}`; basis `|S>`, `S ⊆ {0..n}`;
   532	  `c_k^†|S> = (-1)^{#{l in S : l<k}}|S ∪ {k}>` for `k not in S`, else 0; `F̂ = sum_k c_k^† c_k`.
   533	  Pitfall: dropping the sign breaks `Q^2 = 0` (mutation M3, run in-process).
   534	- **D-koszul-supercharge** (REWORDED per O10/O12). On the **finite-particle core** `R ⊗ Λ` of
   535	  `F ⊗ Lambda(C^{n+1})`, `Q = sum_k a_k ⊗ c_k^†` (D-mode-operators, D-fermionic-modes);
   536	  `Q^2 = 0` exactly; `Q` maps block `(i,N)` to `(i+1,N-1)` and preserves `j = N+i`. With
   537	  `P = ⊕_N P_{0,N}` the **degreewise direct-sum** ground-space projector and `P̂ = P ⊗ 1`, the
   538	  restriction `q = Q P̂ = P̂ Q P̂` is well defined because `W` is `a_k`-invariant. Under the
   539	  conjugate-linear Fock pairing `(W ⊗ Lambda, q)` is the **conjugate dual** of the Koszul
   540	  complex of `R/I` on the variables. Pitfall: `Q^†` does not restrict; its restriction is
   541	  `sum_k Z_k ⊗ c_k` (D-compressed-multiplication). `a_k, Q, L` are unbounded on the completion.
   542	- **D-betti-laplacian** (REWORDED). Globally on `W ⊗ Lambda`, `L_W = q q^† + q^† q`, which
   543	  preserves each internal-degree sector `j` and each block `(i,N)`, `N + i = j`. On a fixed `j`
   544	  sector, `L_W = j P̂ - X X^†` with `X = P̂ Q (1 - P̂)`; hence `0 <= L_W <= j P̂` and
   545	  `||L_W|| <= j`. A block may have `L_W|(i,N) = 0` (no positive spectrum); such a block admits
   546	  no gap and no gap promise. Pitfall: `L_W != P̂ L P̂`, which is the scalar `j P̂`.
   547	- **D-graded-betti-number** (REWORDED per O1/O9). `beta_{i,j}(R/I) = dim Tor_i^R(R/I,C)_j`;
   548	  `beta_{i,j} = 0` for `i > n+1` and for `j - i > reg(R/I)`, where
   549	  `reg(R/I) = max{j-i : beta_{i,j} != 0}` and `reg(I) = reg(R/I) + 1` for a nonzero proper
   550	  homogeneous ideal. `beta_{1,j}` counts minimal generators of `I` in degree `j`; `beta_{2,j}`
   551	  counts the degree-`j` minimal relations **in a minimal free resolution**, equivalently among
   552	  a **minimal homogeneous presentation** — the quotient `Syz/m Syz` of an arbitrary tuple's
   553	  syzygy module is *not* `beta_2` (counterexample `(x,x)`). `Syz(I)_N` (D-syzygy-module) is a
   554	  tuple invariant, not a Betti number.
   555	- **D-betti-gap** (REWORDED per O7). For a block with `L_W|(i,N) != 0`,
   556	  `g_{i,N} = lambda_min^{>0}(L_W|(i,N)) = (N+i) - lambda_max^{<N+i}(X X^†)`, normalised
   557	  `g_{i,N}/(N+i)`. It is an invariant of the **ideal and the Fock metric** (C1); the word
   558	  "presentation-dependent" is withdrawn — only the cost of realising `P_0` through `H_N`
   559	  (`Delta_N`, `alpha_BE`) depends on the generating tuple. Pitfall: not comparable to `Delta_N`
   560	  (proved counterfamily, Step 5.6); undefined on a vanishing block.
   561	- **D-normalised-betti-fraction** (REWORDED per O2/O6). Two distinct ratios, and they must not
   562	  be conflated. *Ambient*: `beta_{i,j}/(M_N C(n+1,i))`, `M_N = dim R_N`. *Conditional on `W_N`*:
   563	  `beta_{i,j}/(HF_{R/I}(N) C(n+1,i))`, defined only when `HF(N) > 0`. These are **numerical
   564	  ratios**, not automatically DQC1-style observables: the ambient one is the zero-mode weight of
   565	  the ambient maximally mixed state; the conditional one additionally requires a normalised
   566	  state on, or preparation access to, `W_N` (weight `HF(N)/M_N` from the ambient state).
   567	- **D-generator-koszul-supercharge** (REWORDED). For positive-degree homogeneous
   568	  `f_1,...,f_d`, `Q_f = sum_j M_{f_j} ⊗ c_j` with **fermionic annihilators** `c_j` on
   569	  `Lambda(C^d)`, fermion `j` carrying internal weight `deg f_j` (a weighted internal grading).
   570	  On the finite-particle core `Q_f^2 = 0`; the fermion-number-zero Laplacian block is
   571	  `sum_j M_{f_j} M_{f_j}^† = H` (D-hamiltonian). Only the **zero-mode dimensions** of the higher
